                <pb facs="0927" n="831" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg831"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.48/1365: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner at Constantinople</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bristol</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-02-01T19:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 1,
                                1921—7 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 3—1.10
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>41. Department’s 3, January 13, 8 p.m.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d803-f1"/> After
                    evacuation of Crimea French Government took over available assets of Wrangel
                    government to help cover expenses of caring for refugees. These assets include
                    war and merchant vessels of which French Government with Wrangel’s consent has
                    now sold four minor vessels. Majority of Wrangel fleet is under French control
                    in port of Bizerte.</p>
                <p>According to statement of local Russian mission supplies belonging to Wrangel
                    government valued at more than 100,000,000 francs have been taken over by the
                    French. Friction has resulted from French action in seizing and disposing of
                    some of this property without granting Russians facilities for checking total
                    value.</p>
                <p>Particulars by mail. Repeated to Paris.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bristol</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
